<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth falls to 15.66 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth falls to 15.66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth fell to 15.65 percent on August 2, 1996, from 16.03 percent a fortnight ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	Aug 2, 1996	July 19,1996     Aug 4, 1995</p>
<p>	    15.65	     16.03		 21.12</p>
<p>Broad money supply was 6,270.75 billion rupees on August 2, 1996 against 6,255.42 billion rupees a fortnight ago and compared to 5,421.86 billion rupees on August 4, 1995, RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
